A||||73||Joe Torma||Fiero Book Submission Form...LOOK!||||4||
Z||000000||Joe Torma||09-01-2001||11:11 PM||||I've put together a form for the Fiero book I've talked about.  Let me know what you think.  I'm still working on it...it isn't functional yet.<P>For those who don't know...I want to put together a book of Fieros and their owners, with lots of pictures and mods plus a writeup if you like.  Pictures and (your own) writeup will be accepted by email/mail.  This form reserves your spot in the book and the info will be put on your page.<P>I would appreciate your input...<BR>1)What should we call the book<BR>2)Anything else to include on the form<BR>3)Any other ideas<P>Thanks!!!<BR> Edit, to minimize confusion...new address: <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> <BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Cheever3000||09-01-2001||11:18 PM||||First thing that comes to mind doesn't even apply to me, but the "model" might need to take into consideration kits or combinations of the body styles you have listed.<P>Otherwise looks really great!<P>Oh, I see you have "rebody" under the Category heading, but still that's not a separate issue than the body style.  I have no suggestions for improvement, so just ignore me.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||09-02-2001||03:23 PM||||Geez, look at all the replies...thanks cheever.  <P>Ok, so I guess we won't make the book.  'thought some of you were interested.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000003||85ZainoGT||09-02-2001||03:35 PM||||ok. question... im all for it but... my car is totally stock right now, but in about 2 months, it will be painted with diff rims, diff interior... will you be able to change it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||09-02-2001||05:13 PM||||Yes, the book will actually be a binder--so nobody has to be left out.  If you change something on your car, send some new pics and update the form and it will be included in future updates.  You can show an evolution of your car if you like!  <P>Cost?  Maybe $10-20 initially--depends on how many pages in the inital publication.  It includes the first cars and the binder. The updates would be like $5 also depending on the size.<P>I really think a big ol book of awesome Fieros would be cool...You can show off to friends...add your own picture pages--and show off at non-Fiero shows.<P>  Yeah, yeah, we have web pages and the forum's pic post--they are free.  Save Ciff some MB's & bandwidth.  I'm sure we all still buy magazines, right?  I'll add a spot on the page for your web site on your page too.<P>C'mon guys a little more enthusiasm would be appreciated.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000005||Dslice||09-02-2001||05:30 PM||||This sounds like a really cool idea, Id consider buying one. Maybe you could put together a electronic E-Book version on CD too. <P>------------------<BR>Rick<P>86GT<BR>84COUP<BR>http://home.mn.rr.com/gmfierogt||||reg||1
